Subject: [PATCH] ath11k: nss: deliver EAPOL exceptions to the wireless interface

The NSS vdev interface defines a separate EAPOL exception packet type.
The special receive callback currently drops it as an unsupported type,
preventing the host authenticator or supplicant from receiving these
handshake frames.

Use the existing receive delivery helper after decapsulation. This also
retains the AP-side PAE group address handling used by normal NSS receive.

--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/nss.c
@@ -978,6 +978,10 @@ ath11k_nss_vdev_special_data_receive(struc
 	}
 
 	switch(wifi_metadata->pkt_type) {
+	case NSS_WIFI_VDEV_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_EAPOL:
+		ath11k_nss_deliver_rx(arvif->vif, skb, eth_decap,
+				      data_offs, napi);
+		break;
 	case NSS_WIFI_VDEV_EXT_DATA_PKT_TYPE_WDS_LEARN:
 		if (eth_decap) {
 			wds_metadata = &wifi_metadata->metadata.wds_metadata;
